step("x6-prot",X6,"Here is a protractor with most of its marks hidden. The straight angle is divided into 180 little units of one degree. There is a long mark at every 10 degrees and a medium mark at every 5. Look at angle K A L. Counting the marks between A K and A L gives 30 degrees. Angle W A L is 50 degrees, and angle T A K is 120 degrees. Because the marks come in tens and fives, you can count in 10s and 5s instead of one by one.","இதோ பெரும்பாலான கோடுகள் மறைக்கப்பட்ட ஒரு கோணமானி. நேர்கோணம் 1 டிகிரி கொண்ட 180 சிறு அலகுகளாகப் பிரிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளது. ஒவ்வொரு 10 டிகிரிக்கும் நீண்ட கோடு, ஒவ்வொரு 5 டிகிரிக்கும் நடுத்தரக் கோடு. ∠KAL ஐப் பாருங்கள். AK க்கும் AL க்கும் இடையிலான கோடுகளை எண்ணினால் 30 டிகிரி. ∠WAL = 50°, ∠TAK = 120°. கோடுகள் பத்து, ஐந்துகளாக இருப்பதால் ஒவ்வொன்றாக எண்ணாமல் 10, 5 எனத் தாவி எண்ணலாம்.",[["clear","","",{}]]+sh(["ptB","ptA"]+["pt%d"%i for i in range(37)],0.02,0.012,"show",200)+sh(["prT","prTl","prW","prWl","prL","prLl","prK","prKl","prA"],0.5,0.03)+sh(["pk1"],0.7,0)+wr_if if False else [["clear","","",{}]]+sh(["ptB","ptA"]+["pt%d"%i for i in range(37)],0.02,0.012,"show",200)+sh(["prT","prTl","prW","prWl","prL","prLl","prK","prKl","prA","ptN"],0.5,0.03)+sh(["pk1","ptK"],0.7,0.05)+sh(["pk2","ptW"],0.8,0.05)+sh(["pk3","ptT"],0.9,0.05))
